===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰer- (yearn)}}
[[Image:Tamil girls group.jpg|thumb|right|A group of '''girls''' in Sri Lanka.]]
From {{inh|en|enm|gerle}}, {{m|enm|girle}}, {{m|enm|gyrle|t=young person of any gender}}, of uncertain origin. Probably from {{inh|en|ang|*gyrle}}, {{m|ang|*gyrele}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gurwilaz}}, a diminutive form of {{der|en|gem-pro|*gurwijaz}} (compare {{cog|frr|gör|t=girl}}, {{cog|nds|Gör}}, {{m|nds|Göre|t=child of any gender}}, {{cog|de|Göre|t=young child}}, dialectal {{cog|no|gorre}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|garre}}, {{m|sv|gurre|t=small child}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰer-|t=short}}<ref>''Webster's New World Dictionary of the American Language'', s.v. "girl" (New York: Simon and Schuster, 2002).</ref> (compare {{cog|sga|gair|t=short}}, {{cog|grc|χρεώ|t=need, necessity}}, {{m|grc|χρήσθαι|t=to need}}, {{cog|sa|ह्रस्व|t=short, small}}).

